{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009453-exotic-materials-ideas","id":1009453,"title":"Exotic Materials Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-28T13:19:21-08:00","id":1009453,"title":"Exotic Materials Ideas","content":"I haven't seen as many exotic materials as I feel there could be, so let's come up with some together! Bonus points for materials that can be made by lower-powered mages. I'm not super-clear on how many Sphere dots you'd need, but I've got some approximations.<br /> <br /> <b>Sovereign Glue</b><br /> The Solificati have long held the formula for this incredibly strong adhesive. Anyone or anything that gets stuck to this paste needs to get 5 successes on a Strength roll to break free. More potent forms can require more successes. This idea may or may not have been stolen from D&amp;D. Probably Matter 2 or 3?<br /> <br /> <b>Poly-Synthetic Fabric</b><br /> A simple and elegant answer to any Etherite's fashion needs, this flexible and strong cloth can be made to withstand mundane cuts and piercing damage, downgrading damage one step so long as its from an edged or piecing weapon. The force of the blow itself isn't diminished, but it is spread out to prevent breaking the skin. Mundane aggravated damage becomes lethal, lethal becomes bashing, and bashing gets ignored completely. Magic or sufficiently advanced scientific cutting/piercing damage is treated as normal (unless Prime is included in the cloth's creation). I think this would be Matter 4 to make the cloth super-durable?<br /> <br /> <b>Cold Stone</b><br /> By combining Matter and Forces, an alchemically treated stone can absorb the heat from the air around it. It chills the area at about the same rate as an open window on a winter day, which makes it great for getting through hot summers for environmentally conscious mages (or older mages who don't yet trust air conditioners). The only problem is the effect cannot be &quot;turned off&quot; without ending the effect entirely. Matter 2 and Forces 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","user":"OmegaZ","date":". 11-28-2016, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}